Description: Credential and sensitive data scanner for SMB, FTP, and local filesystems
 Impacket port of Snaffler, a post-exploitation tool that discovers readable
 SMB shares, FTP servers, and local directories, walks their trees, and
 identifies credentials and sensitive data.
 .
 Features include NTLM and Kerberos authentication, DFS namespace discovery,
 FTP/FTPS scanning, local filesystem scanning, regex-based file and content
 classification with 103+ built-in rules, archive peeking (ZIP/7z/RAR),
 share writability detection, dynamic AD user discovery, triage severity
 levels (Black/Red/Yellow/Green), auto-resume via SQLite, live web dashboard,
 export/import of scan results, and multiple output formats (plain, JSON, TSV).
